WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.200
-Our next guest is
a four-time Super Bowl champion

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.400
and one of the greatest tight
ends to ever play the game.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.634
He's partnering with FanDuel
for the Kick of Destiny

00:00:10.634 --> 00:00:12.000
on Super Bowl Sunday.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.534
Please welcome Rob Gronkowski.

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:19.801
-♪ One nation under a groove ♪

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:24.067
♪ Gettin' down just for
the Gronk of it ♪

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:26.801
♪ One nation,
Gronk on the move ♪

00:00:26.801 --> 00:00:30.067
♪ Nothin' can stop us now ♪

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:32.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.834 --> 00:00:36.334
♪ One nation under a groove ♪

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:38.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:41.267
-That's how you do it!

00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:43.033
That's how you do it
right there!

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:45.000
Rob Gronkowski!

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.100
Gronk, it's always
great to see you, dude.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.200
You're the best, man.
-Thank you, man.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.133
-Come on.
You're always so fun.

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:54.667
They love you, too. Come on.
[ Crowd cheering ]

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:56.801
Big games yesterday.
You did a great job, by the way.

00:00:56.801 --> 00:00:58.467
I saw you on --
-Oh, thank you, man.

00:00:58.467 --> 00:01:00.701
-So, now it's set, though.
Super Bowl is set.

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:03.167
It is Eagles versus Chiefs.

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:04.200
What does Gronk
think about this?

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.367
-Oh, man.

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:08.501
Well, first off,
the Eagles kind of, you know,

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.033
got, like,
a free pass yesterday,

00:01:10.033 --> 00:01:12.901
like, a get-out-of-jail card
for free.

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:14.300
Everything went
their way yesterday.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.601
I was at the game.

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:17.300
I mean, I'm not saying
that they didn't deserve it.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.100
They definitely dominated
the number-one defense

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.501
in the league.

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:23.033
And they dominated the Giants
before -- the week before.

00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:24.567
I'm sorry.
I know we're in New York.

00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:26.801
But -- And Kansas City --
they did enough.

00:01:26.801 --> 00:01:28.434
They're always scrambling.
They always get the job done.

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:29.801
They definitely do.

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:32.801
You know, Patrick Mahomes always
rolling around the pocket.

00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:34.501
Travis is always open.

00:01:34.501 --> 00:01:36.467
They just get it done. They do.

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:40.267
And I would say Philadelphia
has been playing

00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:43.267
more like a team
throughout the whole season.

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:45.434
I'm going to go with the Eagles.
Yes.

00:01:45.434 --> 00:01:46.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:46.634 --> 00:01:48.934
-Wait.
-Yeah.

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:52.501
-That totally changed right --
As you were saying it,

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:53.734
I was like, "Wait.

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:55.634
He's going non-Eagles.
You're going Chie--"

00:01:55.634 --> 00:01:56.834
You're going with Eagles?
-Yes.

00:01:56.834 --> 00:01:58.133
That's why I'm an analyst.

00:01:58.133 --> 00:02:00.334
You know, I'm throwing you off
and then I go back there

00:02:00.334 --> 00:02:01.567
and then I'm back there

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:03.133
and then, boom,
I hit you with the punch.

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:04.400
-You're perfect.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.667
-Yeah, I played against
the Chiefs many times.

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:08.834
And the Chiefs,
the last Super Bowl they won,

00:02:08.834 --> 00:02:10.567
I was retired,
and now they're back

00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:12.767
in the Super Bowl again,
and I'm retired again.

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:15.334
But when I wasn't retired,
we beat them every time

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:16.634
in the AFC championship game.

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:17.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:20.634
-Wow!
-Or the Super Bowl.

00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:22.367
So, I mean,
that's their formula.

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:24.167
I've just got to retire.

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:26.234
-You are a fun human being.

00:02:26.234 --> 00:02:28.200
I love you playing on the field,

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:31.033
but, also, off the field,
you're always fun.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:32.767
I read somewhere
that you said that you believe

00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:34.801
your partying
made you a better player.

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:37.634
-Yeah. Yes. In ways.
So, I've always said that.

00:02:37.634 --> 00:02:41.200
You know, it was kind of, like,
my past, the partying.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.400
You know, everyone's like,

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.567
"Rob, you're partying too much"
or whatever.

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:44.601
I just had a good time
growing up.

00:02:44.601 --> 00:02:45.767
I'm from Buffalo.

00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:47.567
As you can see,
the Bills Mafia --

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:50.000
You watch -- The Bills Mafia --
they're tailgating.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.834
They're jumping off RVs
into tables, breaking them.

00:02:52.834 --> 00:02:54.701
-And breaking tables.
-That's how I grew up.

00:02:54.701 --> 00:02:57.567
Like, I'm from Buffalo.
So, we love to have a good time.

00:02:57.567 --> 00:02:59.501
We love to do crazy things
like that.

00:02:59.501 --> 00:03:01.634
And then I realized -- Like,
I was telling everyone like,

00:03:01.634 --> 00:03:03.067
"It makes me better if I party.

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:05.000
Like, I'm a better player
out on the field."

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.634
And then I realized it
and then I went back

00:03:06.634 --> 00:03:08.100
and I was like, "How do I party?

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.734
Well, I'm carrying my friends,
you know, throughout the bar.

00:03:10.734 --> 00:03:12.000
I'm holding them up.
I'm lifting them.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.567
I'm curling them.
They're on my back.

00:03:13.567 --> 00:03:16.267
I'm jumping up and down
and I'm dancing the whole time,"

00:03:16.267 --> 00:03:18.667
Kind of like Austin Butler,
I'm gyrating like that.

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:19.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:19.801 --> 00:03:23.467
Yes, yes, yes.
And that's helping you --

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:25.234
-Yes. And then I realized
that that

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:27.400
translated to
the football field.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.300
-Yeah, of course it does. Yeah.
-Yes.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:32.501
-How close were you to
suiting up again this season?

00:03:32.501 --> 00:03:36.634
-Um, I was, mm...kind of close.
-Really?

00:03:36.634 --> 00:03:39.534
-Like, you know, I miss it
sometimes, but not really.

00:03:39.534 --> 00:03:41.267
Then I missed it
for like an hour

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:43.167
and then I would go work out
and then I'd be like,

00:03:43.167 --> 00:03:44.334
"Nah, I don't miss it.

00:03:44.334 --> 00:03:46.467
I don't have the energy
to even work out."

00:03:46.467 --> 00:03:48.200
And then, actually,
I had a couple phone calls

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:51.534
about like with six to seven
weeks left in the season,

00:03:51.534 --> 00:03:53.033
and I took them serious.

00:03:53.033 --> 00:03:54.634
I was like,
"Oh, what do you guys got?

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.367
Like, you know,
what's your offers?"

00:03:56.367 --> 00:03:58.133
Like -- I was like, "Alright,
I'll get back to you."

00:03:58.133 --> 00:04:00.601
And I took
a five-day period to see

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:02.267
if I really wanted to go back,
because, I mean,

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:03.400
I've been doing that
my whole life.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:04.634
I've been an athlete
my whole life.

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:06.133
I've been playing football
my whole life.

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:09.400
So you can't pass on
that opportunity, you know?

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.067
I know, I mean,
I just played last year,

00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:12.634
so I was like,
"Okay, I still got it.

00:04:12.634 --> 00:04:15.400
I mean, I can if I really put
my mind to it."

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.534
And those five days passed,
and after the fifth day,

00:04:17.534 --> 00:04:20.367
I was like, "I didn't even think
about going back once.

00:04:20.367 --> 00:04:21.667
I ain't going back."
-Really?

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:22.834
-So I called them
and I was like,

00:04:22.834 --> 00:04:24.634
"Thank you for the opportunity,"
the couple teams.

00:04:24.634 --> 00:04:26.434
And I said, "Appreciate the
love, but I'm fine."

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:28.501
-So there were a
couple of teams trying to get --

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:31.000
-"I'm happy where I am.
I'm content where I am."

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.968
So -- And I'm still
very content with that call.

00:04:33.968 --> 00:04:35.534
And I'm here now.

00:04:35.534 --> 00:04:37.434
I wouldn't be here now if
I wasn't retired.

00:04:37.434 --> 00:04:38.968
-Yeah, exactly.
We're happy you're here.

00:04:38.968 --> 00:04:40.734
Yeah, we want you to be
here whenever you can.

00:04:40.734 --> 00:04:43.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
We love you.

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:45.834
But I know Tom Brady --

00:04:45.834 --> 00:04:48.400
you guys are good pals off
the field, as well.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.133
Did Tom call you up
and be like,

00:04:50.133 --> 00:04:51.501
"Hey, there's always
a spot here for you"?

00:04:51.501 --> 00:04:54.234
-Yes. You know, I love Tom.

00:04:54.234 --> 00:04:56.100
You know, he's a great guy.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.701
He definitely always leaves
the door open, though.

00:04:57.701 --> 00:04:58.834
That's for sure.

00:04:58.834 --> 00:05:01.434
You know, "Buddy,
you know, "I support you.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:04.734
I love you, man, babe,
you know?"

00:05:04.734 --> 00:05:08.133
-That's how he talks?
-Yeah.

00:05:08.133 --> 00:05:09.667
"I love the way
that you play, though.

00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:11.400
You know you're
my favorite tight end.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:13.367
Like, you can
come back anytime."

00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:15.400
-Babe?
-"I support you big-time.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.467
But you know I love
throwing you the ball,

00:05:17.467 --> 00:05:20.234
so come back Week 12,
you know, or something."

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:21.601
-That's a pretty good Tom Brady
right there.

00:05:21.601 --> 00:05:22.734
That's not bad.

00:05:22.734 --> 00:05:23.868
-He definitely
supports you, though,

00:05:23.868 --> 00:05:25.267
and he definitely,
you know, supports me

00:05:25.267 --> 00:05:26.667
throughout the year
if I'm playing football

00:05:26.667 --> 00:05:27.767
or I'm not playing football.

00:05:27.767 --> 00:05:29.267
-He's a good guy.
-Yes. He's a great guy.

00:05:29.267 --> 00:05:31.767
-I don't know if you saw -- he
does a great impression of you,

00:05:31.767 --> 00:05:33.400
weirdly enough, speaking of --

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:36.367
Yeah, I'd like -- If you haven't
seen it, please watch.

00:05:36.367 --> 00:05:38.133
-Dude, that was great.

00:05:38.133 --> 00:05:40.300
That was perfect.
That was just what I needed.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:42.033
I feel ripped now.

00:05:42.033 --> 00:05:44.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:44.334 --> 00:05:47.334
-You didn't say -- That's not --
You didn't say "dude" once.

00:05:47.334 --> 00:05:48.467
-No, no.

00:05:48.467 --> 00:05:50.000
-You haven't said "dude"
once on this show.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.133
That's not a good impression.

00:05:51.133 --> 00:05:53.133
-I mean, you know,
that's kind of, like,

00:05:53.133 --> 00:05:56.634
my macho football, you know --
Gronk, macho football Gronk.

00:05:56.634 --> 00:05:58.734
"Dude, throw me the ball!
I'm wide open."

00:05:58.734 --> 00:06:00.100
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:02.467
-But, yeah, you know,
Tom does a great impression.

00:06:02.467 --> 00:06:05.467
Julian Edelman, though -- he
does even a better impression.

00:06:05.467 --> 00:06:06.534
He does a great job at --

00:06:06.534 --> 00:06:07.834
-Oh, we'll have to get
Edelman on it

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:09.300
and we'll get him to do that.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:11.534
I want to mention your charity.

00:06:11.534 --> 00:06:14.334
The Gronk Nation Youth
Foundation
does incredible work.

00:06:14.334 --> 00:06:15.868
You're doing something
in Boston very soon.

00:06:15.868 --> 00:06:17.100
Can you talk to me about that?

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:20.067
-Yes. So, the Gronk Nation
Youth Foundation --

00:06:20.067 --> 00:06:21.734
we started about 10 years ago.

00:06:21.734 --> 00:06:25.133
We're actually about to be on
the 10-year anniversary of it.

00:06:25.133 --> 00:06:26.634
And, you know, I just had

00:06:26.634 --> 00:06:28.567
an unbelievable
childhood growing up.

00:06:28.567 --> 00:06:31.067
I had three older brothers,
one younger brother.

00:06:31.067 --> 00:06:32.601
We lived in a great neighborhood

00:06:32.601 --> 00:06:34.868
in the suburbs
of Buffalo, New York.

00:06:34.868 --> 00:06:36.868
And I always had someone
to play with,

00:06:36.868 --> 00:06:38.300
if it was my older brothers,

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:40.267
if it was
my older brothers' friends,

00:06:40.267 --> 00:06:42.868
if it was my friends,
if it was my younger brother,

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:44.934
if it was my dad, if my mom.

00:06:44.934 --> 00:06:46.200
It just didn't matter.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:47.968
I had someone to play with
at all times.

00:06:47.968 --> 00:06:51.100
So I wanted every kid
that I could touch

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:52.434
have that opportunity.

00:06:52.434 --> 00:06:55.067
So I started the
Gronk Nation Youth Foundation,

00:06:55.067 --> 00:06:57.200
and it gives kids that don't
have that opportunity,

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:58.501
like, if they don't have
equipment,

00:06:58.501 --> 00:07:01.667
to go out and play football
or go play baseball.

00:07:01.667 --> 00:07:03.934
We donate the equipment
to that organization then

00:07:03.934 --> 00:07:06.534
so they have that opportunity to
go out and get better

00:07:06.534 --> 00:07:08.934
and go out and have fun
and play sports

00:07:08.934 --> 00:07:10.300
and do the right thing as a kid,

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:12.234
like the opportunity
that I had growing up.

00:07:12.234 --> 00:07:14.234
-That's awesome.
And they're doing one in Boston.

00:07:14.234 --> 00:07:15.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yes, yes.

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.400
So -- Oh, so -- Yes.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:20.267
So, currently, the big thing
we're doing right now

00:07:20.267 --> 00:07:24.133
is that there's
a playground on Esplanade.

00:07:24.133 --> 00:07:25.334
That's where the land is.

00:07:25.334 --> 00:07:26.701
And it's right on
the Charles River.

00:07:26.701 --> 00:07:29.234
It's the prime spot in Boston.

00:07:29.234 --> 00:07:31.334
There's a playground,
but we're taking it over

00:07:31.334 --> 00:07:33.033
and we're building the
Gronk Playground right now.

00:07:33.033 --> 00:07:34.534
It's gonna be done
next year in the summer.

00:07:34.534 --> 00:07:36.234
And it's gonna be super-cool.

00:07:36.234 --> 00:07:37.534
There's gonna be a 40-yard dash,

00:07:37.534 --> 00:07:38.834
where the kids
can race each other.

00:07:38.834 --> 00:07:40.267
And what's so neat
about it, too, is that

00:07:40.267 --> 00:07:43.334
there's a football spiked
into the ground

00:07:43.334 --> 00:07:45.767
and there's slides coming off
that football for the kids.

00:07:45.767 --> 00:07:47.234
-[ Laughs ] Come on.
-Yes.

00:07:47.234 --> 00:07:50.901
-See? You're getting involved.
I love that you're doing that.

00:07:50.901 --> 00:07:53.033
Alright, so, I'm watching
the games yesterday

00:07:53.033 --> 00:07:57.100
and I see this commercial
for FanDuel,

00:07:57.100 --> 00:08:00.467
and it's like,
"Gronk, the Kick of Destiny,"

00:08:00.467 --> 00:08:03.033
which is --
I go, "What is this?"

00:08:03.033 --> 00:08:06.267
You're going to kick --
try to kick a field goal?

00:08:06.267 --> 00:08:08.968
-I'm not going to try.
I'm going to kick a field goal.

00:08:08.968 --> 00:08:10.567
Yes. Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:10.567 --> 00:08:11.667
-I apologize.

00:08:11.667 --> 00:08:13.567
-So, I'm teaming up
with FanDuel,

00:08:13.567 --> 00:08:16.901
and the whole, entire project
is called Kick of Destiny

00:08:16.901 --> 00:08:18.334
because it's basically
my destiny,

00:08:18.334 --> 00:08:19.968
because if I don't make it,
I'm going to basically

00:08:19.968 --> 00:08:22.033
get a beating
from everyone in America

00:08:22.033 --> 00:08:23.767
that places a bet on
the Super Bowl game.

00:08:23.767 --> 00:08:24.901
-So, what do you mean?

00:08:24.901 --> 00:08:27.734
So, if you miss the kick,
then what happens?

00:08:27.734 --> 00:08:30.968
-Oh, I'm not missing the kick.
I have no -- I can't miss.

00:08:30.968 --> 00:08:32.934
-But have you ever kicked
a football before?

00:08:32.934 --> 00:08:35.133
-Yes, I have
kicked a football before.

00:08:35.133 --> 00:08:36.734
I've done Punt, Pass, and Kick
when I was a kid

00:08:36.734 --> 00:08:37.834
and I actually made --

00:08:37.834 --> 00:08:40.734
-How old were you?
-9. 9, 10 years old.

00:08:40.734 --> 00:08:43.234
-So since 9 years old,
have you kicked a football?

00:08:43.234 --> 00:08:45.834
-Yes, I kicked one field goal
in high school.

00:08:45.834 --> 00:08:47.000
I was actually the guy that --

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:49.167
I was the kicker-offer in
high school.

00:08:49.167 --> 00:08:50.434
I always -- I used my toe.

00:08:50.434 --> 00:08:52.767
I just ran full speed to
the ball and kicked it,

00:08:52.767 --> 00:08:54.834
and it went to
like 5-yard line every time.

00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:57.667
But then we tried
one field goal, and I made it.

00:08:57.667 --> 00:09:00.801
I'm 100% in my career
kicking field goals,

00:09:00.801 --> 00:09:03.567
and it was a 33-yarder.

00:09:03.567 --> 00:09:05.267
-Yeah, but that was high school.

00:09:05.267 --> 00:09:06.367
-I know.
-Dude...

00:09:06.367 --> 00:09:07.501
-Yes.
-Dude...

00:09:07.501 --> 00:09:09.067
-Yes, it was high school.
-Dude...

00:09:09.067 --> 00:09:11.334
-But this is for $10 million.

00:09:11.334 --> 00:09:14.234
I have to make it for America,
and I'm going to make it.

00:09:14.234 --> 00:09:15.734
-For America.
-Yes.

00:09:15.734 --> 00:09:16.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:16.801 --> 00:09:17.934
Yes.

00:09:17.934 --> 00:09:19.300
-Well, I figured maybe
we'd try it out

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:22.300
and see what your kicking skills
are like with --

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:23.968
You ever play paper football?

00:09:23.968 --> 00:09:25.133
-Yes.

00:09:25.133 --> 00:09:26.868
Elementary school,
I never paid attention.

00:09:26.868 --> 00:09:29.400
All I was doing was that
Tech Deck and paper football.

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:30.501
-Tech Deck, yeah.
-Yes.

00:09:30.501 --> 00:09:31.634
And did you see me
kick that field goal

00:09:31.634 --> 00:09:32.801
right when I walked out?

00:09:32.801 --> 00:09:33.801
-Yeah, I didn't even know
what that thing was,

00:09:33.801 --> 00:09:34.968
but you kicked it pretty far.

00:09:34.968 --> 00:09:37.434
-That was an Ice Shaker.
It went right through.

00:09:37.434 --> 00:09:39.200
-Was that the Ice Shaker
I gave you as a thank-you

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:40.200
for being on the show?

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:42.234
-No, that was --
[ Laughter ]

00:09:42.234 --> 00:09:44.601
No, it was the one I gave you,

00:09:44.601 --> 00:09:45.834
thanking you for letting me
come on the show.

00:09:45.834 --> 00:09:48.167
-Oh, okay.
Thanks for kicking it.

00:09:48.167 --> 00:09:50.000
I want to see what
your skills are right here.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:51.767
This is the --
You've got to go through,

00:09:51.767 --> 00:09:53.601
right through the posts
right there.

00:09:53.601 --> 00:09:54.734
-Well, are you going to
hold it for me?

00:09:54.734 --> 00:09:55.868
-I'd be honored.

00:09:55.868 --> 00:09:57.701
-Did you do paper football
growing up?

00:09:57.701 --> 00:09:58.968
-No.
-Oh.

00:09:58.968 --> 00:10:00.701
-Did you play football
growing up?

00:10:00.701 --> 00:10:03.434
-No. I tried out for
the football team

00:10:03.434 --> 00:10:04.801
and I think I got mono.

00:10:04.801 --> 00:10:06.467
-Oh.

00:10:06.467 --> 00:10:09.667
-That is not funny, because I
had mono my sophomore year

00:10:09.667 --> 00:10:11.701
in college
and missed three games.

00:10:11.701 --> 00:10:15.234
Yeah, that's not funny, Jimmy.
-No, no, no.

00:10:15.234 --> 00:10:16.467
I missed the whole season.

00:10:16.467 --> 00:10:18.667
I'm sorry to get
into your head there. Yeah.

00:10:18.667 --> 00:10:20.467
Now, what do I have to do
to do this?

00:10:20.467 --> 00:10:22.000
What do we have to do?
-Alright.

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:23.534
You just hold it.
Just hold the top.

00:10:23.534 --> 00:10:25.267
-Like that?
-Alright.

00:10:25.267 --> 00:10:27.000
Alright. Oh, by the way,
I'm going to have that

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:30.667
single-bar face mask
when I kick that field goal.

00:10:30.667 --> 00:10:33.467
Yeah. Like in the movies,
in like the 1980s?

00:10:33.467 --> 00:10:34.834
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. I like that.
-Yes.

00:10:34.834 --> 00:10:37.200
-Alright, here we go.
Gronk, this is it.

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:40.267
-This is for $10 million.
-No, no, this isn't it.

00:10:40.267 --> 00:10:43.200
-Oh, alright.
Yeah, yeah, yeah. Not yet.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.100
[ Drumroll ]

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:47.100
Oh!
-All right, no. You missed it.

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:49.300
Gronk, no, we'll try it again.
Here we go.

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:51.567
Look.
No, no, we've got it again.

00:10:51.567 --> 00:10:52.934
That's what we do.
Alright, here we go.

00:10:52.934 --> 00:10:55.534
I'm setting it up right here.
Hold on. Is that right?

00:10:55.534 --> 00:10:57.534
-Right there, yeah.
-Alright, go, buddy.

00:10:58.400 --> 00:10:59.667
Yes!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:59.667 --> 00:11:03.567
It's good! It's good!
Rob Gronkowski, everybody!

00:11:03.567 --> 00:11:05.234
Check out his Kick of Destiny

00:11:05.234 --> 00:11:07.634
live during
the Super Bowl broadcast.

00:11:07.634 --> 00:11:10.534
We'll be right back with a
performance from Tyler Hubbard!

00:11:10.534 --> 00:11:13.634
Stick around.
That's how you do it, bud.

